In \cite{MM} 
the spaces $H^{1,r}(\gamma)$ were defined and proved to coincide for all 
$1<r<\infty$, with equivalent norms.

We recall that the classical space $H^1(\lambda)$ 
can be characterised as the space of all functions $f$ in $L^1(\lambda)$ whose 
\emph{grand maximal function} 
\begin{equation} \mathcal{M} f(x)=\sup\set{\mod{\phi_t*f(x)}: {\phi\in \Phi},\, t>0}
\end{equation}
is also in $L^1(\lambda)$. Here
 $\Phi=\set{\phi \in C_c^1\big(B(0,1)\big): \mod{D^{\alpha}\phi}\le 1 \:
\mathrm{for} \: \mod{\alpha}=0,1}$
and $\phi_t(x)=t^{-n}\phi(x/t)$.

